      "writtenOn": "2021-02-16T08:35:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tl;dr, if I overwrite mRequests to match the per-app default request that tracks this UID, how do I send callbacks back to the registering app if I don\u0027t have the original network request to use?\n\nI think there may be a challenge with this approach but let me explain.\n\nAssume we have a TRACK_DEFAULT request with no per-app policy set. In this case, this member mNetworkRequestForCallback is null and we have a single NetworkRequest in mRequests for the TRACK_DEFAULT request with the correct UID on the NRI, etc.\n\nNow if a per-app policy is set that includes this TRACK_DEFAULT request\u0027s UID, we are then going to update this TRACK_DEFAULT request and overwrite mRequests with the List of network requests that match the per-app default that is tracking this uid.\n\nNow if I overwrite the mRequest object, wouldn\u0027t we lose the original network request for TRACK_DEFAULT? If I don\u0027t have that, I have no way (AFAIK) to communicate back with the original application since ConnectivityManager will be using the original NetworkRequest on its end to key off of for callbacks. Therefore I need to save a reference to the original Network request for sending callbacks on.\n\nLet me know what you think, but the above was what I was thinking.",
      "parentUuid": "13cc5761_a7715289",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5655,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 5669,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "443ee88f053900cfcea952f81336645a19d63acc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
