      "writtenOn": "2021-02-16T08:35:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure we want to copy the tracking default\u0027s NetworkRequests for all TRACK_DEFAULT?\n\nI.e., you have this being called for all TRACK_DEFAULT:\n\n  private List\u003cNetworkRequest\u003e trackDefaultRequest(uid, packageName) {\n    NRI defaultReq \u003d findDefaultReqForUid();\n    return new NRI(..., copy(defaultReq)... )\n  }\n\nHowever that would copy the default request\u0027s items which are not the same as TRACK_DEFAULT since TRACK_DEFAULT uses this method which will have different NetworkRequest items vs the default request (particular the VPN removal and uid):\n\n   private static NetworkCapabilities createDefaultNetworkCapabilitiesForUid(int uid) {\n        final NetworkCapabilities netCap \u003d new NetworkCapabilities();\n        netCap.addCapability(NET_CAPABILITY_INTERNET);\n        netCap.removeCapability(NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_VPN);\n        netCap.setSingleUid(uid);\n        return netCap;\n    }\n\nTherefore the isPerAppDefaultTrackingUid(nr.getRequestorUid() check makes sure we don\u0027t overwrite that behavior. \n\nAlso, I need to use the new Constructor here since it is the only one that sets the mNetworkRequestForCallback which I need for callbacks. TBH, I actually made most of the changes you originally suggested (minus removal of that check) but then my unit tests started failing and I realized that I still needed this constructor.\n\nThat said, as we have another comment thread specifically on `mNetworkRequestForCallback`, my suggestion would be to resolve that thread and based off of that, we can revisit the above.",
      "parentUuid": "9b7c099e_4b519aca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5981,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 5981,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "443ee88f053900cfcea952f81336645a19d63acc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
