      "writtenOn": "2021-02-16T12:53:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your analysis is right and my explanation lacking. I was thinking copy() would do this work of removing the NOT_VPN flag and resetting the uid.\n\nAll requests tracking a default have this in common ; they have their own UID instead of the UID of the real default NRI (the one in mDefaultRequests), and they don\u0027t have NOT_VPN. In fact, that\u0027s also true of the multi-layer track-defaults, that\u0027s what they also should do.\n\nSo in my mind, copy(defaultReq) would look like :\n\n  private NetworkRequest copy(defaultReq, uid) {\n    final NR nr \u003d new NR(defaultReq);\n    nr.networkCapabilities.removeCapability(NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_VPN);\n    nr.networkCapabilities.setSingleUid(uid);\n    return nr;\n  }\n\nIn fact, that should even be used in requestNetwork instead of createDefaultNetworkCapabilitiesForUid. Today it looks almost incidental that the existing TRACK_DEFAULT work, they just have a custom function returning tailor-made caps that lets them share fate with the default request, but it would be much clearer if l.5368 (in PS4) was to call copy(mDefaultRequest, uid).\n\nWould this solve you concern ?",
