      "writtenOn": "2021-02-15T11:38:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Um no, you do need to update them all. Let\u0027s posit the following scenario :\n\n- Google Maps files a TRACK_DEFAULT\n- Later, a policy starts applying to Google Maps\n\n...we need to update its TRACK_DEFAULT to the new one.\n\nThankfully in this case, it just means simpler code, as you can just remove l.9585~9588. I also discuss in another comment how to reduce l.9577~9584 to a simple check. In the end, I think this method can be as simple as :\n\n  new List\u003c\u003e\n  for (nri in mNetworkRequests) {\n    if (nri.tracksDefault) add()\n  }\n  return\n\n(which the stream API would let you write in a readable one-liner, but you can\u0027t do that)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9587,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 9587,
        "endChar": 100
      },
      "revId": "443ee88f053900cfcea952f81336645a19d63acc",
