      "lineNbr": 9587,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-16T12:53:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah-ha ! So it\u0027s the other way around. I thought this was checking before the requests have been filed, but IIUC from your comment, we come here after the new default requests (that correspond to the new policy) have been filed. That makes sense, now that I think about it.\n\nWell then you have the reverse problem.\n\n- A policy is installed making Google Maps go on the OEM_PAID network.\n- Google Maps files a TRACK_DEFAULT.\n- A new policy in installed where Google Maps is not present.\n\nIn this case, this won\u0027t match – Google Maps\u0027 request should track the regular default network. And so we won\u0027t include it in the returned list, we won\u0027t update its TRACK_DEFAULT, and it will continue to believe its default network is the OEM_PAID network.\n\nNo ?",
      "parentUuid": "a2545acf_2668ab1c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9587,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 9587,
        "endChar": 100
      },
      "revId": "443ee88f053900cfcea952f81336645a19d63acc",
